## Posts
- [Front\-End Web Deep Dive: Runtime Config](https://www.heroku.com/blog/front-end-web-deep-dive-runtime-config/): Runtime configuration has been brought to the Front\-End Web Cloud Native Buildpack in a way that is standard, secure, and requires zero re\-builds\. By revisiting Twelve\-Factor principles through the lens of modern web standards, we have created a strategy that works for any framework\.
- [Improved Static Website Support on Heroku with Front\-End Web Cloud Native Buildpack](https://www.heroku.com/blog/improved-static-website-support-with-front-end-web-cloud-native-buildpack/)
- [October 2026 Update: Heroku Innovations and New Features](https://www.heroku.com/blog/october-2026-update-heroku-innovations-features/)
- [A New Era for Managed Databases: Announcing Heroku Postgres Advanced](https://www.heroku.com/blog/new-era-managed-databases-announcing-heroku-postgres-advanced/): At Heroku, we’ve built a platform that allows developers to focus on their apps, not managing their infrastructure\. Heroku Postgres Advanced carries forward that philosophy as our next\-generation database offering, available today\.
- [Introducing Team Authorizations](https://www.heroku.com/blog/introducing-team-authorizations/): \<p\>Team Authorizations let you create and manage API tokens and OAuth authorizations at the team and team’s resources level instead of tying them to one person’s account\.\</p\>

\<p\>Until now, every API token belonged to an individual\. When that person left the team, changed roles, or lost access, any integration, CI/CD pipeline, or automation built on their token could break without warning, and nobody else could easily see what was at risk\. Team Authorizations fixes that\. Your integrations keep running no matter who's on the team\.\</p\>

